WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.968
We are hanging out with Ice-T,
right here!

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:09.033
Now...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.434
You're known to say
the blunt truth,

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:12.934
so I thought you could
settle some of

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:15.100
the biggest and most important
debates of all time.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.901
Are you ready to do this?
-Absolutely.

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.701
-Alright. It is time for
"Ice-T Settles It."

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.601
-♪ Ice-T settles it ♪

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:25.334
♪ Ice-T settles it ♪

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:31.133
-Okay. First up, blocking
or muting someone on Twitter?

00:00:31.133 --> 00:00:32.701
-Mute them.

00:00:32.701 --> 00:00:34.934
A lot of people get off
because they got blocked.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:38.534
They -- Dummies write that off
as a badge --

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:39.801
You know what I call them.
-Yep.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:40.868
-Dumb [bleep]
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:43.300
-They get off
as a badge of honor.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.300
"Ooh! I got blocked by Ice-T.
I'm important."

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.968
But if you mute them,
they don't know they're blocked,

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:52.267
and then they just yell off into
the Twitter void of nothingness.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.767
They think
they're talking to you.

00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:56.234
-Right?
-Yeah.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.634
-Don't give them that --

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:00.534
-Hit that "mute" button
and let them yell into nothing,

00:01:00.534 --> 00:01:02.167
and nobody gets to
hear them again.

00:01:02.167 --> 00:01:03.300
Okay.
-I love it.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.334
Number two, here we go.
How about this?

00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:09.067
Slow Walkers or slow talkers?

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.701
-I hate slow talkers,

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.868
you know,
even though I rap slow.

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:14.534
But I don't have time --
I'm like,

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:15.767
"Speed it up, get to the point.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.067
Like, what are you
talking about?"

00:01:17.067 --> 00:01:19.701
I always do that with Coco.
I'm like...

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.667
"I know there's
a punch line coming.

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:23.133
Come on with it. Let's go."

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:25.133
Yeah, slow talkers drive me
bananas.

00:01:25.133 --> 00:01:26.968
-I was behind, though,
a family this morning.

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.334
I was walking into work.

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:31.234
And it was -- They are the
slowest-walking family ever.

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:32.634
And I love that
they're a family,

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.767
and that's great and everything,
but there was like five of them.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.701
And they really --
They were almost on the edge,

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:37.934
almost by the street.

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.734
They just had
the whole sidewalk blocked off.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:42.200
-Yeah, I get that.
Well, I'm a slow walker, though.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.601
You know, players --
we walk slow.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.234
We in no rush.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:47.734
-Oh, no. I walk like this.

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.667
-That's how you...
♪♪

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:51.934
-That's how I walk.
That's how I walk.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:54.501
-Players walk like this.
♪♪

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:56.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.000
-We probably
walked by each other, yeah.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.601
-Yeah, you don't want to
mess up your shoes.

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:10.367
You got to keep everything
together, you dig?

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.133
-How about this?
Should you reheat spaghetti?

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.534
-Yeah. Why not?
-I know.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:15.701
I think it tastes --
-Why not?

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.667
I mean, it's good.
If it was good spaghetti.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:20.734
If it was bad spaghetti,
it might turn into antimatter.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.334
I don't know.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.200
-You ever had fried spaghetti?

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.734
-You fry spaghetti?

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:28.067
-Check it out.

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.567
-No. Hey, you learn something
new on "Jimmy Fallon."

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:31.801
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.501
-Alright, how about this?
Ready?

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:35.767
PlayStation or Xbox?

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:39.968
-Oh, man, you trying to mess
with some of my sponsorships.

00:02:39.968 --> 00:02:42.968
-No, no, no.
I would never do that.

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.100
-I mean, you know,
I actually have both systems.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.167
-Yeah, I know.

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.400
-You know, they fight --
like, gamers --

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.801
But now they actually
have cross-platform playing,

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.501
where you can be on --

00:02:52.501 --> 00:02:54.234
-Either one?
-Yeah.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:58.133
So, I'm a gamer, but -- Yeah,
I had to have both of them

00:02:58.133 --> 00:03:01.334
because some games exclusively
come out on the games first.

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:04.067
And I want them, so, you know --
One time, I told the people --

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.601
I said,
"I have two gaming consoles."

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.200
Like, "That's 'cause
you're rich."

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.000
It's not like it's two Bugattis.
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.734
-No, yeah, no. I understand.
-It's a damn gaming console.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:13.100
-It's not like a
Bentley or Lamborghini, yeah.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.267
-Take it easy, people.
-Take it easy.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:19.100
"Call of Duty" or "Halo?"

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.734
-"Call of Duty."
-There you go.

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:22.434
-Only reason is 'cause
I'm not really a space guy,

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.634
even though I play "Destiny."

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.901
But I'm not into -- And, also,

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:29.234
I missed the
learning curve on "Halo."

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.501
"Call of Duty" is more real.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:33.968
You run around with guns,
get it in.

00:03:33.968 --> 00:03:36.434
-Okay.

00:03:36.434 --> 00:03:39.067
Greatest rap album of all time.

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:41.334
-Ooh!
-That's difficult.

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:44.200
-I say "Paid in Full"
by Eric B. &amp; Rakim.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:47.234
-Wow! Wow! I love that.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.234 --> 00:03:48.534
-Why that one?

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:50.801
-Because that was the
most influential album to me

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:51.934
when I was making my album.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.601
I'll say
"Fear of a Black Planet"

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:56.033
with Public Enemy
would be a close second,

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:58.734
and then
"Straight Outta Compton," N.W.A,

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.334
would be the top three.

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.000
But each one of those albums

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.901
had a lot to do with influencing
me as an emcee.

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.167
But when I heard Rakim,

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.000
I had never heard
nobody rap like that.

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.467
And it was so many hits
on that album.

00:04:11.467 --> 00:04:13.033
Get "Paid in Full,"

00:04:13.033 --> 00:04:14.968
and you'll bang it
all the way to the house.

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:17.100
-Eric B. &amp; Rakim. Love that.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.634
-Gucci or Chanel?

00:04:19.634 --> 00:04:21.267
-Well, my daughter's
named Chanel.

00:04:21.267 --> 00:04:24.934
This is a trick question.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:27.367
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I got to go with Chanel.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:28.767
She's probably gonna
watch this and think --

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:31.801
-Yeah. Hi, Chanel.
-But she likes Gucci, too.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.267
You know, she -- We messed up.

00:04:33.267 --> 00:04:35.200
I mean, we could have
named her anything.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.701
We decided to name her something

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.868
that's going to break us
down the line, you know?

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:40.501
-Yeah, exactly, right?

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:42.067
-Because Coco -- So, it was

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:43.701
kind of play off of
Coco and Chanel.

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.334
So, yeah, that's what's up.

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:46.801
-How about this one then,
if she's watching?

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.367
"Dora" or "Peppa"?

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:49.968
-"Peppa Pig."

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.367
-Alright.
-Straight up, "Peppa Pig."

00:04:51.367 --> 00:04:52.701
-Wow!

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:56.334
-"Peppa Pig" has Chanel
talking like she's British.

00:04:56.334 --> 00:04:57.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.901 --> 00:05:00.133
-[ British accent ]
"Muddy puddles."

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.200
-[ British accent ]
Yeah, "muddy puddles."

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.567
-"Muddy puddles."

00:05:02.567 --> 00:05:04.501
-[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, yeah. "Ready, steady.

00:05:04.501 --> 00:05:05.501
Ready, steady."

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:06.667
I'm like,
"It's 'ready, set, go.'"

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:10.501
"No, no, Daddy.
It's ready, steady, go."

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:14.334
-Iced tea --
sweetened or unsweetened?

00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:17.501
-Who drinks
unsweetened iced tea?

00:05:17.501 --> 00:05:19.234
That's some white people [bleep]

00:05:19.234 --> 00:05:21.234
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:26.734
-I was going to say me.
I was going to say me.

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:29.534
"Can I get unsweetened, please?

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.367
♪♪

00:05:31.367 --> 00:05:33.467
I want unsweetened."

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:38.000
-Black people has real --
We drink sweetness.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:41.634
We drink Kool-Aid.
We drink things that taste good.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:44.834
You know?

00:05:44.834 --> 00:05:47.133
And tea is not the place to go
to get healthy anyway.

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:50.100
I mean, you can do green tea,
I get it, if that's your thing.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.567
But unsweetened tea --
that's nasty.

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:53.567
-Okay, here we go.

00:05:53.567 --> 00:05:56.901
Last one, law or order?

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:58.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.734 --> 00:06:03.534
-Well, law is --
Law would be the court, I guess.

00:06:03.534 --> 00:06:04.701
-Yep.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.300
-So it's mother[bleep]
order, cuz, come on.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.467
-Yeah, that's what I'm
talking about.

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:10.534
Come on, that is Ice-T!

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:11.868
My thanks to Ice-T.

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:15.534
